cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use schrodinger-fem, please cite the accompanying manuscript and this archived release."
title: "schrodinger-fem: a finite element solver for the stationary Schrödinger eigenvalue problem in Elmer"
abstract: >-
  A finite element module for the Elmer package that solves the stationary
  Schrödinger eigenvalue problem in one, two and three dimensions, together with
  an independent Python implementation used for code-to-code verification. The
  weak form yields the generalized symmetric eigenproblem A psi = E M psi with
  A = K + M_V, assembled with multilinear Lagrange elements and solved either by
  dense LAPACK factorization or by sparse shift-and-invert Arnoldi iteration.
  The package documents two failure modes that are easy to encounter and hard to
  diagnose: the diagonal-shift treatment of Dirichlet data, which introduces
  spurious eigenvalues, and the dense local assembly that makes the MPI route
  return wrong results. It ships seven benchmark cases with analytic reference
  spectra and the scripts that reproduce every table and figure of the
  accompanying manuscript.
type: software
